00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:09,000
I think it's something that you grow into over time. as I think I've written to you in the past,

138
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Nobody gets the Eagle easy. You become an Eagle. If you earn the Eagle and you're serious about it, you become an Eagle.

139
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:22,000
You may finally become an Eagle when you're 30. You may do it when you're 15..

140
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:26,000
But if you live the Eagle life, you become an Eagle.

141
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:33,000
That's a really good way of looking at it And maybe it'll help inform people who get a little exercised about this every once in a while.

142
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Yeah, I'm weary of that. You know we put enormous stress upon these kids,

143
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:47,000
That sort of unwritten rule that you know your Eagle project now has to change mankind forever.

144
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:54,000
That's an awful lot to put on a teenage boy. Boys are ready to do their Eagle project. when they're ready to do their Eagle project,

145
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:58,000
And not a day before, Not a minute before, Not a minute before,

146
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,000
A minute before, they're terrified. They don't want to do it, They don't want to deal with adults,

147
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:06,000
They don't want to organize anything And then one morning they get up and they decide I'm going to do it,

148
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:09,000
And then they're focused and they pull it off.

