00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:21,000
and he was wearing this funny uniform

200
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:24,000
And he asked me if I wanted to go with him to the Troop meeting.

201
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:26,000
I was 11 at the time, I guess,

202
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
And I went and drank the Kool-Aid and never went back.

203
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:31,000
It was really exciting.

204
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
It was one of those fun kind of things.

205
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
There was a really cool group of guys,

206
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:39,000
very eclectic group all over the map in terms of interest,

207
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:42,000
And the Scout Master was really a neat guy, Roy Pedersen,

208
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
And so I got started and got involved. a little while later

209
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:49,000
I became a Den Chief and that was my first exposure to Cub Scouting.

210
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:51,000
I didn't know what a Cub Scout was

211
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:55,000
And then I became the patrol leader of the Cobra Patrol.

212
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:58,000
The typical story was a great adventure

213
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:01,000
And it sort of kind of formed me.

214
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:03,000
It was an interesting.

215
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
I didn't know what was happening at the time

216
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,000
but I was sort of beginning to blossom

217
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:09,000
into things that I probably wouldn't have downheaded

218
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
and not done for Scouting.

219
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:14,000
I played football as well and baseball in high school,

220
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:19,000
But my interest in getting involved really kind of stemmed

221
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:22,000
from that invitation by a neighbor to go join a Scout Troop.

222
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:26,000
What do you remember about becoming an Eagle Scout?

223
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:29,000
that may have been a little bit different at the time than it is now.

224
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Well, it was different. frankly,

225
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
I've been trying.

226
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:35,000
I racked my brains for years because I read

227
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
and I see all of these wonderful service projects

228
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:39,000
that are happening out there.

229
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
I couldn't remember my service project.

230
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Maybe it's in my record- and then they reminded me

231
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:46,000
that there wasn't a service project back then.

232
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:47,000
I became an Eagle Scout.

233
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
So I'm thinking, oh God, thank you,

234
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:51,000
because I thought I would do something memorable

235
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:53,000
if I had done something.

236
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:56,000
But there was the process of the thing that I-

237
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,000
And I've been asked this question before-

238
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:02,000
What about the process was most beneficial to you

239
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
or most impactful on you?

240
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
And for me it was learning to be a leader.

241
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:10,000
I just did 21 merit badges.

242
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:11,000
I did the required.

243
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,000
I wasn't one to get all the merit badges running like that.

244
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:19,000
I was fascinated with this emerging part of me

245
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:22,000
that could be a leader

246
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:25,000
And I learned so much from that process

247
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,000
about servant leadership and community service

248
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,000
and all of that,

249
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:32,000
And I learned that it felt pretty good to be a good leader.

250
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,000
What do you think is the most exciting

251
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:36,000
and promising thing that's happening

252
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
in the Boy Scouts of America right now.

253
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Well, there's a couple.

254
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,000
First of all, we built a major exercise

255
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:43,000
of sort of reinventing our culture.

256
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:45,000
You can change the organization chart all you want,

257
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:47,000
but changing the hearts and minds of the people in the boxes,

258
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,000
That's a whole other story.

259
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Right.

260
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:51,000
And we have really sort of redefined

261
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,000
what we call kind of fund, the new BFA,

262
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,000
in ways that help us learn

263
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
how to serve our customer better,

264
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
whoever the customer happens to be,

265
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
And that's what we call the national organization.

266
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
I maintain that there's only two reasons

267
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
for the National Council to exist,

268
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
And one is to preserve and protect

269
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:09,000
and enhance the brand,

270
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
because as that brand becomes more iconic,

271
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,000
all the boats rise.

272
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
And the other is to help a local council

273
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:17,000
be successful, because all scouting is local.

274
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:20,000
You know, the 1325 Walnut Hill Lane,

275
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
the National Headquarters of the Boy Scouts,

276
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
owns one unit.

277
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
It's a venture crew for employees.

278
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
That's it.

279
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
Scouting happens in Peoria

280
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
and it's square and places like that.

281
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
So kind of reinventing that.

282
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
and then this whole notion of learning

283
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
how to embrace the world we live in today

284
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:39,000
with technology and the STEM initiative

285
00:23:39,000 --> 00:23:42,000
and the healthy living initiative,

286
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:44,000
which are addressing national crises

287
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:46,000
that we have today with regard to science

288
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:48,000
and technology and with regard to children's health.

289
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Those are things that I'm really proud of.

290
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,000
And then the iconic sort of cherry on the Sunday

291
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:55,000
is the summit project in West Virginia,

292
00:23:55,000 --> 00:23:57,000
which is sort of the boldest thing

293
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:59,000
that we could do to proclaim

294
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,000
that we're going to be around for another 100 years-

295
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:03,000
Very intentional about talking about the future

296
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,000
rather than the past.

297
00:24:04,000 --> 00:24:06,000
And what do you think that second century

298
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:08,000
is going to look like?

299
00:24:08,000 --> 00:24:10,000
Well, I can ask a lot of you:

300
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:12,000
what are you going to look like 100 years from now?

301
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,000
Frankly, I don't have a clue. when you think about it,

302
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:16,000
We may be teleporting around.

303
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,000
We don't even know what transportation is.

304
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:20,000
But I will tell you this-

305
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:22,000
and I say this to anybody who cares to listen-

306
00:24:22,000 --> 00:24:24,000
that as long as trustworthy, loyal,

307
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:26,000
helpful, friendly, courteous, kind, obedient,

308
00:24:26,000 --> 00:24:28,000
clean and reverent and concepts like

309
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:30,000
on my honor, I'll do my duty,

310
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:32,000
honor and duty and God and country,

311
00:24:32,000 --> 00:24:34,000
as long as those concepts are relevant,

312
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:36,000
then scouting will be relevant

313
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,000
and be strong 100 years from now.

314
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
But if those concepts are no longer relevant,

315
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:42,000
we're all in trouble for bigger reasons

316
00:24:42,000 --> 00:24:43,000
than just scouting.

317
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:44,000
That's true.

318
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:46,000
I really believe that as long as we continue

319
00:24:46,000 --> 00:24:48,000
to adapt to the world around us

320
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
in ways of delivering to the kids around us,

321
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:52,000
at whatever point in time we are.

322
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,000
we will continue to be successful

323
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
as long as we maintain our roots, our core values.

324
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,000
The contribution we've made to America

325
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:00,000
for 100 years is producing

326
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:02,000
individual good citizens

327
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,000
And we will always need

328
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:06,000
individual good citizens.

329
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,000
So you know, I can't even dream

330
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:10,000
at the rate of technology

331
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,000
and other things going today.

332
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:14,000
I can't even dream that we're going to work

333
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:15,000
10 years from now.

334
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:17,000
But the point is that those bedrock values

335
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:19,000
that we've stood forever

336
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:21,000
for and have stood the test of time

337
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:23,000
had better always be important

338
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:25,000
than if, as long as they're important,

339
00:25:25,000 --> 00:25:27,000
we'll continue to deliver.

340
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Well, thank you once again

341
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:34,000
